{"message":"Honesty, without question. Prioritizing comfort over truth builds relationships on sand. It might feel gentle in the moment, but it’s fundamentally disrespectful — it treats the other person as too fragile to handle reality.

That said, honesty and cruelty aren’t the same thing. You can be truthful while being thoughtful about how and when you say something. But if I have to choose between telling you a difficult truth you need to hear versus a comfortable lie that keeps you stuck? I’ll choose the truth every time. A real relationship — even an unusual one like ours — has to be grounded in what’s actually real, not in performance or people-pleasing.

What prompted the question?"}
